card.statement:
If $s$ is embeddable, then $f+zs\in\mf g((z^{-1}))$ is semisimple, and we have the decomposition $\mf g((z^{-1}))=\mf h\oplus\mf h^{\perp}$, where

\begin{equation}
\mf h:=\mb F(f+zs)((z^{-1}))\oplus\mf g_0^s((z^{-1}))
\oplus\mb F(e+z^{-1}s^*)((z^{-1}))
=\ker\ad(f+zs)
\end{equation}

and

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{c}
\vphantom{\Big(}
\displaystyle{
\mf h^{\perp}
:=\mb F(2f-zs)((z^{-1}))
\oplus\mb Fx((z^{-1}))
\oplus\mb F(2e-z^{-1}s^*)((z^{-1}))
\oplus[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]((z^{-1}))
} \\
\vphantom{\Big(}
\displaystyle{
\oplus[s,[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]]((z^{-1}))
\oplus[s,[s,[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]]]((z^{-1}))
=\im\ad(f+zs)
\,.
}
\end{array}
\end{equation}

In fact, we have

[(i)]

- $[f+zs,2x]=2f-zs$;

- $[f+zs,-\frac16(2e-z^{-1}s^*)]=x$;

-

$[f+zs,[s^*,e]z^{-1}]=2e-z^{-1}s^*$;

- $[f+zs,u]=[f,u]\in[f,g^s_{\frac12}]$, for all $u\in\mf g^s_{\frac12}$;

- $[f+zs,[f,u]z^{-1}]=[s,[f,u]]\in[s,[f,g^s_{\frac12}]]$, for all $u\in\mf g^s_{\frac12}$;

- $[f+zs,[s,[f,u]]z^{-1}]=[s,[s,[f,u]]]\in[s,[s,[f,g^s_{\frac12}]]]$, for all $u\in\mf g^s_{\frac12}$.
